KINESIS DECISION TREE:
├── Just deliver data A → B?          → Firehose
├── Need sub-second processing?        → Flink
├── Need multiple independent consumers? → Enhanced fan-out
├── Hot shards / throttling?           → Fix partition key
└── High latency on Firehose?          → Tune buffer size/interval

GLUE FIXES:
├── Column not found?                  → Re-crawl (stale catalog)
├── Slow JDBC reads?                   → hashfield/hashexpression
├── Reprocessing old files?            → Job Bookmarks
├── Too many small files on read?      → groupFiles/groupSize
└── Exactly-once in streaming?         → Checkpointing

GLUE BATCH vs STREAMING:
├── Batch: Job Bookmarks (track processed files)
└── Streaming: Checkpoints (track processed offsets)

MIGRATION TO REDSHIFT:
├── Small dataset (< 1 TB)?           → DMS direct to Redshift
└── Large dataset (multi-TB)?          → DMS → S3 → COPY command


FIREHOSE CHEAT SHEET:
├── Destinations: S3, Redshift, OpenSearch, Splunk, HTTP (NOTHING ELSE)
├── Dynamic partitioning: YES (inline JQ or Lambda metadata)
├── Format conversion: YES (JSON → Parquet/ORC, needs Glue Catalog schema)
├── Min latency: 60 seconds (buffer interval)
├── Cannot read FROM S3 (ingestion only)
└── Cannot write TO DynamoDB, RDS, or Kinesis



KINESIS THROUGHPUT (per shard):
├── Write: 1 MB/sec | 1,000 records/sec
├── Read (no fan-out): 2 MB/sec SHARED across all consumers
└── Read (enhanced fan-out): 2 MB/sec PER consumer (dedicated)

INGESTION SERVICE SELECTOR:
├── SFTP/FTP files from partners  → AWS Transfer Family
