5. Cost Optimization Patterns

COMPUTE COST:
├── Glue: Auto Scaling (enable it!) — scales DPUs down when idle
├── EMR: Spot instances on task nodes (up to 90% savings)
├── Redshift: Reserved Instances (1-3 year) for steady workloads
├── Redshift Serverless: Pay per RPU-hour (bursty workloads)
├── Athena: Pay per TB scanned → use Parquet + partitioning to reduce scan
└── Lambda: Pay per invocation + duration (free tier: 1M requests/month)

STORAGE COST:
├── S3 lifecycle policies (Standard → IA → Glacier)
├── S3 Intelligent-Tiering (auto-moves between tiers)
├── Redshift: Concurrency Scaling (auto-adds clusters for burst queries)
├── Delete/archive old data (retention policies)
└── Compress data (Parquet/ORC vs CSV = 75% less storage)



QUERY COST (ATHENA):
├── Use columnar format (Parquet/ORC) — scan only needed columns
├── Partition data — scan only needed partitions
├── Compress data — less bytes scanned
├── Use LIMIT — doesn't help cost (Athena scans full partition anyway)
└── Workgroups with query cost limits (prevent runaway queries)

EXAM TRIGGER:
